finishersRank":21,"finishRateRank":88,"winningTimeRank":10,"winningTimeRankDir":7,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1966,"mensWinner":"Tommy MALONE","mensTime":"06:14:07"}},"narrative":"The 2001 Comrades Marathon was the 76th running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.600 km. The race was held on Saturday, 16 June. Conditions: Cool at start. Mild to warm later. Runners had 11 hours to complete the course.\n\nAndrew KELEHE claimed the men's title in 05:25:52, ahead of Leonid SHVETSOV (05:26:29) and Vladimir KOTOV (05:27:22). Elvira KOLPAKOVA won the women's race in 06:13:54, followed by Deborah MATTHEUS (06:23:04).\n\nElvira KOLPAKOVA's 06:13:54 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1966 (Tommy MALONE, 06:14:07).\n\nFrom a field of 15,350 entries, 11,080 runners crossed the finish line (72.2% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 9,421 men and 1,659 women (15.0% female). The average finish time was 09:39:23.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 731 Silver, 2,502 Bill Rowan, 7,827 Bronze. 1,830 runners (16.5%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Joseph VENTER in 11:00:00.\n\nCompared to the previous down run in 1999, the field was 8.7% larger.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 42% of the finishers, with 6,410 seniors (avg 09:32:33) and 4,670 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}